{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbKGhUboJ5h7jiF5wrC3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote and checked the candidate, **`short_pattern_evenness_lapse`**. The self-check printed `OK`, but its fit scored far below the current best model. It also ran the one smoke check only, with no full fit.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people expect a random coin to produce every short pattern about equally often:\n- heads and tails,\n- the four flip pairs (HH, HT, TH, TT),\n- the flip triples.\n\nA sequence looks non-random when a few short patterns dominate it. A streak is all HH; strict alternation is all HT and TH. The model scores this as how far the spread of overlapping one-, two- and three-flip patterns falls short of the most even spread the sequence's length allows. How much that unevenness matters is each person's own trait, drawn from a population, and people guess on some trials at a personal lapse rate.\n\nThis is a different kind of process from anything in the set. The current models add up separate cues (alternation rate against a personal ideal, heads/tails balance, streaks, palindromes). This one uses a single rule: a random sequence should use its short patterns evenly. Because of that, it penalises both streaks and rigid alternation. The models built on a personal ideal switching rate can instead reward alternation for some people.\n\n**Fit:** the check loaded the file, found a finite log-probability on the real responses, and confirmed the data contract. A short MCMC run (one chain, 100 draws) gave an ELPD-LOO of −2702.3. The current best model is at −2333.8, so this candidate trails by about 370 nats. It is unlikely to beat the incumbent and is mainly useful as a new mechanism for the next design to test.\n\n**Not yet known:**\n- **Convergence:** a single chain cannot report R-hat, so convergence is unverified until admission's full fit.\n- **Reliability of the score:** the −2702.3 may be inaccurate. 1.9% of trials had a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance, which could be noise from the short run.\n- **Novelty:** the check does not test whether the model's predictions differ enough from the existing models.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2911,"cache_read_input_tokens":65963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2911,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea869f4c-c822-4fee-b610-6c2b5e15c28f","uuid":"cc10182c-da83-4a00-bf14-a97fce7252a5","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:55:23.581Z","request_id":"req_011CfbKGgnv8ULKrWay5NG8U"}
